<div class="page-break"></div><h1>Padma Inventory — Technical System Documentation</h1>
<p><strong>Project:</strong> <code>padma_inventory</code> <strong>Purpose:</strong> Padma Bank Limited IT asset / inventory management (stock in, stock out, branch inventory, employee assignment, reporting, procurement support). <strong>Stack:</strong> Laravel 12, PHP 8.2+, Blade, jQuery/Bootstrap (backend UI), Oracle (production via <code>yajra/laravel-oci8</code>) or MySQL (local/XAMPP).</p>
<p>&gt; <strong>Module-wise docs &amp; structure:</strong> see <a href="./README.md">docs/README.md</a>, <a href="./STRUCTURE.md">STRUCTURE.md</a>, and <a href="./modules/">docs/modules/</a>. &gt; <strong>Word file:</strong> <a href="./word/Padma_Inventory_Module_Documentation.doc">docs/word/Padma_Inventory_Module_Documentation.doc</a> (regenerate: <code>php docs/build_word_doc.php</code>).</p>
<hr>
<h2>1. System overview</h2>
<p>The application is a monolithic Laravel web app. Business logic lives in <strong>Controllers</strong>, data access in <strong>Repository implementations</strong> bound to <strong>Interfaces</strong> in <code>RepositoryServiceProvider</code>. Most inventory state is stored in a central <strong><code>item_inventory</code></strong> table (and related master tables), differentiated by <strong><code>store_type</code></strong> and reference numbers (<code>set_uniq_no</code>, <code>stock_in_no</code>, <code>stock_out_no</code>).</p>
<pre>
flowchart TB
    subgraph ui [Web UI]
        Blade[Blade views]
        Routes[routes/web.php]
    end
    subgraph app [Application layer]
        Ctrl[Backend Controllers]
        Repo[Repository Impl]
        Support[Support classes]
    end
    subgraph data [Data]
        Oracle[(Oracle / MySQL)]
        HRM[Padma HRM API]
    end
    Blade --&gt; Routes --&gt; Ctrl
    Ctrl --&gt; Repo
    Ctrl --&gt; Support
    Repo --&gt; Oracle
    Ctrl --&gt; HRM
</pre>
<hr>
<h2>2. Technology stack</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Layer</th><th>Technology</th></tr>
<tr><td>Framework</td><td>Laravel 12</td></tr>
<tr><td>Language</td><td>PHP 8.2+</td></tr>
<tr><td>Auth</td><td>Laravel UI (<code>Auth::routes</code>), session-based login</td></tr>
<tr><td>DB drivers</td><td>MySQL (dev), Oracle OCI8 (typical production schema <code>PAD_INVENTORY</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Excel/CSV</td><td><code>maatwebsite/excel</code>, <code>PhpOffice/PhpSpreadsheet</code> (branch upload mapper)</td></tr>
<tr><td>PDF</td><td><code>barryvdh/laravel-dompdf</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Barcode</td><td><code>milon/barcode</code>, <code>picqer/php-barcode-generator</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>API auth (optional)</td><td>JWT (<code>tymon/jwt-auth</code>), Sanctum</td></tr>
<tr><td>Social login</td><td>Laravel Socialite (Google/Facebook controllers present)</td></tr>
</table>
<p><strong>Key Composer packages:</strong> see <code>composer.json</code>.</p>
<hr>
<h2>3. Project structure</h2>
<pre>
padma_inventory/
├── app/
│   ├── Http/Controllers/Backend/   # Feature controllers
│   ├── Http/Controllers/Auth/      # Login, password reset
│   ├── Interfaces/Repo/Backend/    # Repository contracts
│   ├── Repository/Backend/         # Repository implementations
│   ├── Models/                     # Eloquent models (subset of tables)
│   ├── Support/                    # Cross-cutting helpers (SET_UNIQ_NO, CSV mapper, stock refs)
│   ├── Traits/                     # UserAccessTraits, CommonTraits (HRM API)
│   └── Providers/RepositoryServiceProvider.php
├── routes/web.php                  # All primary HTTP routes
├── resources/views/backend/        # Admin/inventory UI
├── database/migrations/            # Laravel migrations + some .sql scripts
└── docs/                           # This document and related guides
</pre>
<hr>
<h2>4. Architecture patterns</h2>
<h3>4.1 Repository pattern</h3>
<p>• <strong>Interface:</strong> <code>app/Interfaces/Repo/Backend/{Feature}Repo.php</code></p>
<p>• <strong>Implementation:</strong> <code>app/Repository/Backend/{Feature}RepoImpl.php</code></p>
<p>• <strong>Registration:</strong> <code>app/Providers/RepositoryServiceProvider.php</code></p>
<p>Controllers depend on interfaces; implementations extend <code>EloquentBaseRepository</code> where applicable.</p>
<h3>4.2 Access control</h3>
<p>• <strong><code>UserAccessTraits::userAccessFunction()</code></strong> resolves menu slug from URL and loads <strong><code>access_menu</code></strong> row for the user’s <strong><code>user_types</code></strong> (view/add/edit/delete flags).</p>
<p>• Controllers call <code>$this-&gt;userAccessFunction()</code> and pass <code>$userAccessData</code> to views.</p>
<p>• Many backend controllers use <code>$this-&gt;middleware(&#039;auth&#039;)</code>.</p>
<h3>4.3 Multi-tenancy scope</h3>
<p>Most queries filter by <strong><code>org_id</code></strong> from <code>auth()-&gt;user()-&gt;org_id</code> and often <strong><code>branch_id</code></strong> / <strong><code>hr_branch_id</code></strong> on the <code>branch</code> table.</p>
<hr>
<h2>5. Core data model</h2>
<h3>5.1 Master data</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Table / area</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>organization</code></td><td>Organization master</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>branch</code></td><td>Branches; links to HR via <code>hr_branch_id</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>division</code>, <code>department</code></td><td>Org structure</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>category</code> / <code>categories</code></td><td>Item categories (<code>category_title</code>, <code>category</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>brand</code> / <code>brands</code></td><td>Brands</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>supplier</code> / <code>suppliers</code></td><td>Suppliers</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>item_info</code></td><td>Item master (title, category, brand, image, etc.)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>unit</code></td><td>Unit/size master</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>users</code>, <code>user_types</code></td><td>Application users</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>backend_menu</code>, <code>access_menu</code></td><td>Menu and RBAC</td></tr>
</table>
<p>&gt; Note: Legacy naming mixes singular table names in queries (<code>item_info</code>, <code>category</code>) with migration names (<code>items</code>, <code>categories</code>). Code predominantly uses <strong><code>item_info</code></strong> and <strong><code>item_inventory</code></strong>.</p>
<h3>5.2 Inventory fact table: <code>item_inventory</code></h3>
<p>Single table holds stock positions and movement-related rows. Important columns (conceptual):</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Role</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>org_id</code>, <code>branch_id</code></td><td>Scope</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>item_id</code>, <code>category_id</code>, <code>brand_id</code>, <code>supplier_id</code></td><td>References</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>store_type</code></td><td><strong><code>SP</code></strong> = stock position / package row (inventory entry), <strong><code>SI</code></strong> = stock in transaction, <strong><code>SO</code></strong> = stock out transaction</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>set_uniq_no</code></td><td>Device/set identifier (e.g. <code>PBL-DK-5007</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>stock_in_no</code>, <code>stock_out_no</code></td><td>Document references</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>uniq_serial_no</code></td><td>Hardware serial</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>quantity</code>, <code>price</code>, <code>condition</code>, specs (<code>ram</code>, <code>storage</code>, <code>processor</code>, …)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>from_employee_id</code>, <code>to_employee_id</code>, branch/division from/to</td><td>Assignment &amp; movement</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>warehouse</code>, <code>remarks</code>, <code>status</code></td><td><code>status &lt;&gt; 9</code> typically means active</td></tr>
</table>
<p><strong>Design rationale:</strong> Stock in and stock out share one table; reports filter on <code>store_type</code> and reference numbers. See <code>STOCK_IN_OUT_IMPLEMENTATION.md</code> and <code>SCHEMA_RECOMMENDATIONS.md</code>.</p>
<h3>5.3 Audit / movement logs</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Table</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>item_transfer_logs</code></td><td>Employee-to-employee transfer within branch (from <code>/transfer-items</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>item_swap_logs</code></td><td>Pending swap between employees; receiver confirms on <code>/receive-swap-items</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>stock_out_gate_pass_logs</code></td><td>Gate pass print audit</td></tr>
</table>
<hr>
<h2>6. Identifiers and codes</h2>
<h3>6.1 <code>SET_UNIQ_NO</code> — <code>App\Support\SetUniqNoFormatter</code></h3>
<p>• Format: <strong><code>PBL-{abbrev}-{sequence}</code></strong> (e.g. <code>PBL-DK-5007</code>).</p>
<p>• Abbreviation derived from item title (desktop → <code>DK</code>, laptop → <code>LP</code>, etc.).</p>
<p>• Sequence scoped per org/branch; considers existing <code>item_inventory</code> rows with <code>status &lt;&gt; 9</code>.</p>
<p>Used by: manual inventory entry, CSV import preview/import, spec component rows sharing one set code.</p>
<h3>6.2 Stock reference numbers — <code>App\Support\StockReferencePrefixBuilder</code></h3>
<p>Builds <strong><code>stock_in_no</code></strong> / related prefixed strings from branch/division tags + <code>set_uniq_no</code>.</p>
<h3>6.3 Item codes</h3>
<p><code>UserAccessTraits::generateRandomItemCode()</code> and item save logic in <code>ItemController</code> generate org-specific item codes from branch/category context.</p>
<hr>
<h2>7. Functional modules</h2>
<h3>7.1 Dashboard</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Route</th><th>Controller</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>/dashboard</code></td><td><code>HomeController</code></td><td>Main dashboard</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>/dashboard-total-count-log</code></td><td><code>DashboardLogController</code></td><td>Aggregate counts</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>/dashboard-*-details</code></td><td><code>DashboardLogController</code></td><td>Category/item/supplier drill-down</td></tr>
</table>
