<hr>
<h2>9. External integration: Padma HRM API</h2>
<p><strong>Trait:</strong> <code>App\Traits\CommonTraits</code></p>
<p>• <strong>Env:</strong> <code>PADMA_HRM_API_URL</code></p>
<p>• <strong>Flow:</strong> Service login → bearer token → GET endpoints such as <code>/api/v3/user-info-padmaportal?emp_id=...</code></p>
<p>• <strong>Used by:</strong> Stock out, transfer, swap, receive flows for employee name, branch, division validation.</p>
<p>Credentials for the API login are configured in code/env; production should use <strong>environment secrets</strong>, not hardcoded values in the repository.</p>
<hr>
<h2>10. Request lifecycle (example: CSV import)</h2>
<pre>
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant C as ItemsCsvUploadController
    participant M as InventorySpreadsheetImportMapper
    participant S as Session
    participant DB as Database

    U-&gt;&gt;C: POST upload (file, branch_id)
    C-&gt;&gt;M: parseFile(path)
    M--&gt;&gt;C: rows, column_map, format
    C-&gt;&gt;C: resolveCategory → IT Equipment
    C-&gt;&gt;C: assignPreviewSetUniqNumbers
    C-&gt;&gt;S: csv_preview_data
    C--&gt;&gt;U: preview.blade.php
    U-&gt;&gt;C: POST storeCsv (edited grid)
    C-&gt;&gt;DB: transaction: item_info, item_inventory, specs
    C--&gt;&gt;U: success + export download
</pre>
<hr>
<h2>11. Configuration and deployment</h2>
<h3>10.1 Environment (<code>.env</code>)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Variable</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>APP_URL</code>, <code>APP_ENV</code>, <code>APP_DEBUG</code></td><td>App base</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>DB_CONNECTION</code>, <code>DB_*</code></td><td>MySQL local or <code>oracle</code> connection</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>PADMA_HRM_API_URL</code></td><td>Employee API base URL</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Oracle-specific: <code>config/oracle.php</code>, package <code>yajra/laravel-oci8</code>.</p>
<h3>10.2 Local development (XAMPP)</h3>
<p>1. PHP 8.2+, Composer install 2. <code>cp .env.example .env</code>, configure DB 3. <code>php artisan key:generate</code> 4. <code>php artisan serve</code> → <code>http://127.0.0.1:8000</code> 5. Run migrations / legacy SQL scripts as required for your DB (<code>add_stock_in_no_to_item_inventory.sql</code>, swap/transfer migrations).</p>
<h3>10.3 Web server</h3>
<p>Point document root to <code>public/</code>. Ensure <code>storage/</code> and <code>bootstrap/cache/</code> are writable.</p>
<hr>
<h2>12. Security notes</h2>
<p>• CSRF on POST forms (<code>VerifyCsrfToken</code>).</p>
<p>• Session authentication for backend routes using <code>auth</code> middleware.</p>
<p>• Menu-level permissions via <code>access_menu</code>; not all routes may enforce granular checks—review per module for hardening.</p>
<p>• File upload: CSV/XLSX size and extension validation in <code>ItemsCsvUploadController</code>.</p>
<p>• HRM API credentials must be rotated and stored in env/secrets manager.</p>
