<h2>15. Document maintenance</h2>
<p>• <strong>Version:</strong> 1.1 (March 2026 — barcode module + A–Z SQL)  </p>
<p>• <strong>Update when:</strong> New routes/modules added, <code>store_type</code> semantics change, CSV category rules change, or Oracle schema migrations applied.</p>
<p>For module-specific deep dives, extend this file or add <code>docs/modules/{module}.md</code>.</p>
<div class="page-break"></div><h1>Module 00 — System Overview</h1>
<h2>Purpose</h2>
<p><strong>Padma Inventory</strong> (<code>padma_inventory</code>) is Padma Bank Limited’s IT asset inventory system: register devices, assign to employees/branches, stock in/out, branch bulk upload, swap/transfer, and reporting.</p>
<h2>Users</h2>
<p>• IT / branch inventory staff  </p>
<p>• Admin (users, menus, permissions)  </p>
<p>• Procurement (requisition, quotation — partial workflow)</p>
<h2>Technology</h2>
<p>• <strong>Backend:</strong> Laravel 12, PHP 8.2+  </p>
<p>• <strong>UI:</strong> Blade, Bootstrap, jQuery  </p>
<p>• <strong>DB:</strong> MySQL (dev), Oracle (production typical)  </p>
<p>• <strong>Integrations:</strong> Padma HRM API (employee lookup)</p>
<h2>Core concept</h2>
<p>Almost all quantity and assignment state lives in <strong><code>item_inventory</code></strong>, split by <strong><code>store_type</code></strong>:</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>SP</code></td><td>Stock position / package (main inventory row + spec rows)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>SI</code></td><td>Stock in document line</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>SO</code></td><td>Stock out document line</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Device identity: <strong><code>set_uniq_no</code></strong> (e.g. <code>PBL-DK-5007</code>), <strong><code>uniq_serial_no</code></strong>.</p>
<h2>Documentation map</h2>
<p>See <a href="../README.md">docs/README.md</a> for all module files and <a href="../STRUCTURE.md">STRUCTURE.md</a> for folder layout.</p>
<div class="page-break"></div><h1>Module 01 — Architecture</h1>
<h2>Pattern</h2>
<p><strong>MVC + Repository</strong></p>
<p>• Controllers: HTTP, validation, session, view data  </p>
<p>• <code>Interfaces/Repo/Backend/*Repo.php</code>: contracts  </p>
<p>• <code>Repository/Backend/*RepoImpl.php</code>: queries &amp; persistence  </p>
<p>• Bindings: <code>app/Providers/RepositoryServiceProvider.php</code></p>
<h2>Cross-cutting</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Component</th><th>Role</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>UserAccessTraits</code></td><td>Menu slug → <code>access_menu</code> (view/add/edit/delete)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>CommonTraits</code></td><td>HRM API token + employee JSON</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>app/Support/*</code></td><td>SET_UNIQ_NO, CSV mapper, stock number prefixes</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Security</h2>
<p>• Session login (<code>auth</code> middleware on most backend controllers)  </p>
<p>• CSRF on POST  </p>
<p>• Org scoping: <code>auth()-&gt;user()-&gt;org_id</code></p>
<h2>Diagram</h2>
<pre>
Controller → Repo Interface → RepoImpl → DB
         ↘ Support helpers
         ↘ Traits (HRM, access)
</pre>
<p>Full structure tree: <a href="../STRUCTURE.md">STRUCTURE.md</a>.</p>
<div class="page-break"></div><h1>Module 02 — Authentication &amp; RBAC</h1>
<h2>Login</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
<tr><td>Routes</td><td><code>/login</code>, <code>Auth::routes([&#039;register&#039; =&gt; false])</code>, <code>/logout</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Controller</td><td><code>App\Http\Controllers\Auth\LoginController</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Views</td><td><code>resources/views/auth/*</code></td></tr>
</table>
